# @NAME@

@DESCRIPTION@

An @KIND@ built on the Sonore SDK: `src/plugin.cpp` becomes a CLAP, a VST3,
an LV2, an Audio Unit (on macOS), a standalone app, and an AAX for Pro Tools
when the build is given Avid's AAX SDK (`-DSONORE_AAX_SDK_ROOT=<the unpacked
SDK>`; Avid gives it to registered developers at developer.avid.com/aax).

## Build

```
cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build --config Release
ctest --test-dir build -C Release
```

@SDK_NOTE@

`ctest` runs the app's offline self-check (`@TARGET@App --verify`: it renders
without a device or a window and fails on silence, NaN or a malformed
descriptor) and, with a source checkout of the SDK, the real-time audit,
which fails on any allocation on the audio thread.

## What comes out

| Output | Where hosts look for it |
| --- | --- |
| `@TARGET@.clap` | Windows `%COMMONPROGRAMFILES%\CLAP`, macOS `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/CLAP`, Linux `~/.clap` |
| `vst3/@TARGET@VST3.vst3` | Windows `%COMMONPROGRAMFILES%\VST3`, macOS `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3`, Linux `~/.vst3` |
| `@TARGET@AU.component` | macOS `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components` |
| `@TARGET@LV2.lv2/` | Windows `%APPDATA%\LV2`, macOS `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/LV2`, Linux `~/.lv2` |
| `aax/@TARGET@AAX.aaxplugin` (Windows), `@TARGET@AAX.aaxplugin` (macOS) | Windows `C:\Program Files\Common Files\Avid\Audio\Plug-Ins`, macOS `/Library/Application Support/Avid/Audio/Plug-Ins` |
| `@TARGET@App` | runs as it is; `--help` lists its options |

## Before you ship

- `@ID@` is this plugin's identity to every host. Pick it for good now:
  changing it later makes every saved session lose the plugin.
- The parameter table is positional. Once a version is out, only append.
- The Audio Unit's codes (`@AU_SUBTYPE@` / `@AU_MANUFACTURER@` in
  CMakeLists.txt) must be unique to you. The AAX is filed under the same two.
- A retail Pro Tools loads only an AAX that Avid has approved and PACE has
  signed: write to audiosdk@avid.com for the signing tools, then sign every
  build with `wraptool`. A developer build of Pro Tools loads it unsigned,
  which is how to test it first.
- Keep the version in `src/plugin.cpp` and in `CMakeLists.txt` the same.
- Run the format owners' validators on the build: clap-validator
  (github.com/free-audio/clap-validator), pluginval
  (github.com/Tracktion/pluginval), and `auval` on macOS.
